WEBVTT

00:15.887 --> 00:18.587
<b>Jaadugar</b>

01:38.637 --> 01:41.767
<b>25 Years Ago</b>

01:53.387 --> 01:56.017
My lady!

01:57.397 --> 01:59.607
My lady!

02:01.527 --> 02:04.937
Gosh. What are you doing out here?

02:04.937 --> 02:07.157
It's time for you to get ready to leave.

02:08.787 --> 02:10.037
I'll be right there.

02:17.827 --> 02:20.517
Farewell, Naiman.

02:23.667 --> 02:28.947
<i>As a member of the Naimans, 
a nation far to the west of here,</i>

02:28.947 --> 02:34.007
<i>I was to marry into the Merkits, 
with whom we shared an alliance.</i>

02:34.527 --> 02:37.837
I wonder what the Merkit tribes are like.

02:37.837 --> 02:42.687
They live in the woods to the north, 
and many are skilled bowmen called Mergen.

02:43.277 --> 02:44.407
Mergen?

02:44.407 --> 02:47.777
They're the Mergen people, 
thus the name: Merkits.

02:48.117 --> 02:50.937
<i>In other words, barbaric hunters.</i>

02:52.187 --> 02:53.197
<i>Well, it matters not.</i>

02:54.357 --> 02:56.167
<i>I am no more than a valuable gift.</i>

02:57.307 --> 03:01.027
<i>No different from a precious gemstone
 or a fine fur pelt.</i>

03:02.017 --> 03:03.137
<i>That's fine by me.</i>

03:04.157 --> 03:07.317
<i>I take pride in that fact.</i>

03:09.107 --> 03:15.017
<b>The Mergen People</b>

03:18.837 --> 03:20.727
<i>So this is where the Merkits live?</i>

03:21.837 --> 03:24.367
<i>It's much drearier than I expected.</i>

03:25.037 --> 03:26.967
<i>Why are there so few men?</i>

03:27.327 --> 03:28.617
Töregene.

03:29.497 --> 03:33.947
<b>Merkit Tribe Chieftain
Dayir</b>

03:29.637 --> 03:33.947
I see you made it here safely. 
I'm sorry this isn't much of a welcome.

03:34.587 --> 03:37.197
Taken aback at learning 
your husband is so senile?

03:37.197 --> 03:38.297
Oh, no.

03:40.947 --> 03:42.377
<i>Well, so be it.</i>

03:43.027 --> 03:45.897
<i>Marrying a much older man
is by no means a rare occurrence.</i>

03:47.907 --> 03:53.747
<i>However, Dayir made no advances 
after we were wed.</i>

03:56.077 --> 03:57.707
<i>On the contrary...</i>

03:58.927 --> 04:00.437
You're away again today?

04:00.707 --> 04:03.397
I'm sorry for always leaving you behind.

04:04.077 --> 04:05.857
And we're moving camp again?

04:06.447 --> 04:08.817
We only just arrived here.

04:10.127 --> 04:12.787
We can't stay in one place for very long.

04:13.147 --> 04:14.857
You'd best get going.

04:15.787 --> 04:16.817
Chuu!

04:20.847 --> 04:22.627
Let me know if you ever need anything.

04:22.627 --> 04:23.767
Y-Yes.

04:24.087 --> 04:24.587
Um—

04:24.587 --> 04:27.767
Mistress. What shall I do with these?

04:27.767 --> 04:29.967
Oh, for those...

04:31.037 --> 04:35.167
<i>Do all of the other tribes 
relocate at such short intervals?</i>

04:35.827 --> 04:39.687
<i>No, there's something strange
 going on here.</i>

04:39.687 --> 04:42.177
<i>It's as if we're fleeing from something.</i>

04:45.277 --> 04:48.897
<i>Well, I suppose there's no use
 in me worrying about it.</i>

04:49.397 --> 04:51.767
<i>My only role is to be a gemstone.</i>

04:52.357 --> 04:55.827
<i>What good would it do 
for a gemstone to worry?</i>

05:00.107 --> 05:02.037
<i>I want to return to Naiman.</i>

05:11.797 --> 05:16.127
<i>No one will notice if I go missing.</i>

05:16.717 --> 05:19.487
<i>Chieftain Dayir won't.
Nor will anyone else.</i>

05:20.347 --> 05:21.597
Wait!

05:23.317 --> 05:24.977
Don't move!

05:32.347 --> 05:33.857
That was a close one.

05:34.097 --> 05:35.497
Are you unhurt?

05:38.667 --> 05:41.257
Qultuqan, you live up 
to your title of Mergen.

05:41.257 --> 05:43.507
Not really. Anyone could've done that.

05:44.107 --> 05:44.827
Oh?

05:45.187 --> 05:47.127
You must be Töregene...

05:47.127 --> 05:49.417
my new mother!

05:52.807 --> 05:55.307
I'm Khulan, Dayir's daughter.

05:55.307 --> 05:58.177
Qultuqan. My name, I mean.

06:00.727 --> 06:05.507
<i>Khulan was Dayir's child, and Qultuqan
was the child of another chieftain.</i>

06:05.827 --> 06:06.647
Look.

06:06.647 --> 06:11.077
If you go down this river, 
it splits into the Qara and Dal Rivers.

06:11.077 --> 06:15.547
Go further downstream still, 
and they feed into the Selenge River.

06:15.547 --> 06:18.377
That's where both Qultuqan 
and I were born.

06:18.377 --> 06:19.717
Oh?

06:19.717 --> 06:24.327
And if you go <i>all</i> the way down the rivers, 
do you know where they end up?

06:27.157 --> 06:30.047
You know the star to the north 
that doesn't move?

06:30.717 --> 06:38.297
Underneath it, there's a great big hole, 
into which all of the world's rivers flow.

06:38.297 --> 06:41.897
Wow, I never knew that.

06:43.427 --> 06:45.847
It's not like you've seen it for yourself.

06:46.107 --> 06:48.167
Hey, Qultuqan.

06:48.167 --> 06:49.347
Is that right?

06:49.347 --> 06:53.187
Neither of us have the power of kams 
to converse with spirits.

06:53.187 --> 06:58.237
Father's a kam, and he's been 
to where the rivers end many times.

06:58.597 --> 07:01.947
His soul turns into a bird
 and flies there.

07:02.447 --> 07:03.537
A kam?

07:04.827 --> 07:08.077
I wish I had kam powers, too.

07:08.077 --> 07:10.707
Or I was more skilled with a bow.

07:10.707 --> 07:12.547
You really <i>are</i> a dreadful shot.

07:12.547 --> 07:14.497
Hey, hold your tongue!

07:14.497 --> 07:15.837
You said it yourself!

07:15.837 --> 07:16.967
Hey!

07:16.967 --> 07:18.347
"Hey!" What?

07:20.227 --> 07:22.027
You're laughing.

07:22.027 --> 07:23.537
Oh, pardon me.

07:29.607 --> 07:33.577
<i>Something changed within me that day.</i>

07:35.987 --> 07:41.307
<i>It felt as though the very world 
around me now stirred my soul.</i>

07:51.997 --> 07:55.167
<i>I experienced laughter and joy.</i>

08:06.527 --> 08:09.827
<i>Discontent and sorrow, too.</i>

08:22.407 --> 08:26.607
<i>I came to love the days I spent here.</i>

08:36.957 --> 08:40.107
<i>Then I understood for the first time.</i>

08:46.527 --> 08:47.597
Wake up, everyone!

08:47.987 --> 08:49.557
Extinguish your hearths!

08:49.557 --> 08:51.327
We need to flee at once!

08:51.327 --> 08:52.227
What's happened?

08:52.227 --> 08:54.507
Our chieftains' armies have been bested!

08:54.507 --> 08:56.607
The enemy will be here soon!

09:04.407 --> 09:06.197
Into the forest!

09:07.807 --> 09:10.847
Khulan! Töregene! This way!

09:10.847 --> 09:11.867
Qultuqan!

09:16.747 --> 09:18.257
How much did they plunder?

09:18.567 --> 09:22.437
Qudu's family is gone, 
as are Chilaun's wife and children.

09:23.537 --> 09:24.927
Töregene!

09:25.297 --> 09:26.757
Father!

09:27.477 --> 09:29.307
You must have been scared.

09:29.307 --> 09:31.767
Thank you for protecting Khulan.

09:32.527 --> 09:34.727
She was the one who protected me.

09:35.037 --> 09:37.057
What exactly is going on?

09:37.697 --> 09:41.487
So the Naimans told you nothing after all?

09:41.937 --> 09:44.567
I suppose I don't blame them.

09:45.887 --> 09:47.867
Our people have an enemy.

09:48.327 --> 09:50.077
Temüjin of the Mongols.

09:51.837 --> 09:55.207
The man they now call Genghis Khan.

09:59.367 --> 10:01.047
Genghis Khan?

10:01.047 --> 10:06.507
We Merkits have long skirmished 
with the Mongols.

10:06.507 --> 10:10.987
They've deprived us 
of many of our family and riches,

10:10.987 --> 10:13.187
as we have done the same in kind.

10:14.347 --> 10:20.147
But that changed with Temüjin as leader,
and the balance of the steppe was lost.

10:21.067 --> 10:25.217
The reason you were given away 
to become the wife of an old man like me

10:25.217 --> 10:28.067
was for the sake of our alliance
 against the Mongols.

10:28.767 --> 10:30.017
However...

10:30.567 --> 10:33.327
The end may finally be near.

10:33.887 --> 10:38.647
Say, Brother. What will become of us 
if we lose to the Mongols?

10:38.647 --> 10:43.767
You need to ask? They'll slaughter the men
 and take the women and children.

10:44.597 --> 10:47.337
I'm scared. I don't want to die.

10:47.687 --> 10:50.567
Fool. And you call yourself a Merkit man?

10:59.767 --> 11:00.937
Usun.

11:00.937 --> 11:02.197
Usun.

11:02.927 --> 11:05.627
Usun. The word for the "flowing river."

11:05.627 --> 11:09.527
The title bestowed by the earth
 upon Father in his role as a kam.

11:10.027 --> 11:13.997
Listen well. No one is to intrude 
until I have finished.

11:15.317 --> 11:19.237
I shall beseech the spirits 
to tell me our future.

11:23.947 --> 11:27.557
<i>Spirits, lift me up to the heavens.</i>

11:27.557 --> 11:30.517
<i>Show me what lies in our future.</i>

12:51.777 --> 12:52.817
Usun!

12:55.767 --> 12:58.097
Khulan, are you there?

12:59.977 --> 13:02.147
I'm right here, Father.

13:02.667 --> 13:05.147
I saw a lush steppe.

13:05.587 --> 13:08.897
A river branching and feeding into many.

13:09.407 --> 13:12.187
And when I followed the river
 to its source,

13:12.187 --> 13:17.487
atop a mountain as tall as the heavens,
I found a pure riverhead.

13:18.347 --> 13:20.687
The rivers are bloodlines 
of the steppe people.

13:20.687 --> 13:25.777
This signifies that Mongol progeny 
will spread across the land.

13:25.777 --> 13:26.667
You mean...

13:26.667 --> 13:29.377
We will lose to the Mongols.

13:32.067 --> 13:35.637
Does that mean we'll all be killed?

13:35.937 --> 13:38.097
No, I won't let that happen.

13:38.637 --> 13:40.917
This is what the spirits say.

13:40.917 --> 13:44.537
The Merkit blood will live on 
even after we surrender to the Mongols.

13:44.537 --> 13:47.957
Will Genghis Khan really show us mercy?

13:48.337 --> 13:53.357
We'll have to give appropriate tribute
 in exchange, of course.

13:53.767 --> 13:55.967
A pure riverhead.

13:55.967 --> 14:00.077
I shall offer my daughter to Genghis Khan.

14:00.077 --> 14:00.857
Khulan.

14:02.847 --> 14:03.457
You mustn't!

14:03.987 --> 14:06.167
I won't allow you to offer up
 Khulan as sacrifice!

14:06.727 --> 14:09.337
She's a human with her own mind and will!

14:09.557 --> 14:11.557
Not a gemstone or a fur pelt!

14:14.547 --> 14:17.667
She's not like me.

14:20.497 --> 14:21.977
Töregene.

14:21.977 --> 14:24.787
Thank you, but I'll be fine.

14:25.377 --> 14:26.447
Khulan?

14:28.357 --> 14:31.367
I'm happy, Father.

14:31.807 --> 14:35.567
I've always resented my womanhood, 
requiring others to protect me.

14:35.567 --> 14:39.777
But now I can serve as the arrow 
that will protect all of you.

14:40.047 --> 14:41.577
You're...

14:41.577 --> 14:43.667
We Merkits are masters of the bow.

14:44.207 --> 14:48.267
Watch as a daughter of the Mergen people
 takes down a wolf.

14:53.607 --> 14:57.467
<i>And so, we surrendered to the Mongols.</i>

14:58.307 --> 15:05.807
<i>Khulan severed the long chains of enmity 
that had bound the Mongols and Merkits,</i>

15:06.287 --> 15:09.067
<i>saving many Merkit lives.</i>

15:12.157 --> 15:18.907
<i>Qultuqan and the other Merkit tribes, 
however, chose defiance to the very end,</i>

15:19.147 --> 15:21.107
<i>fleeing westwards.</i>

15:25.587 --> 15:27.287
That should be everyone.

15:27.287 --> 15:29.207
Why did you summon us all?

15:29.677 --> 15:31.287
<i>There are only young girls here.</i>

15:31.287 --> 15:33.017
Are you Dayir Usun?

15:33.677 --> 15:38.047
We serve Prince Ögedei, 
the third son of the Khan.

15:38.327 --> 15:41.757
Our role is at the rear of the army, 
keeping watch over the supplies.

15:42.157 --> 15:44.897
Sounds like I can rest assured, then.

15:44.897 --> 15:47.227
These women are in your hands now.

15:47.597 --> 15:48.557
Chieftain Dayir?

15:49.487 --> 15:54.027
We've decided to hand all of you 
over to Mongol nobles.

15:54.027 --> 15:55.067
No!

15:55.437 --> 15:57.147
Töregene.

15:57.147 --> 15:58.947
Listen up, all of you.

15:58.947 --> 16:02.897
The Mongols have spared us
 our lives, and no more.

16:02.897 --> 16:06.247
They haven't forgiven us 
for our past confrontations.

16:06.677 --> 16:09.247
We are sure to be reduced to slaves.

16:09.657 --> 16:11.667
But you girls are different.

16:12.247 --> 16:14.987
Life is just beginning for you.

16:14.987 --> 16:17.157
Go and find happiness.

16:19.147 --> 16:20.587
You there.

16:20.867 --> 16:23.557
Make sure you tell your prince 
and your Khan this:

16:23.557 --> 16:27.227
These women are no longer Merkits 
from here on out.

16:27.227 --> 16:29.037
Now and forevermore.

16:29.037 --> 16:30.937
I-I'll pass it on.

16:33.637 --> 16:35.187
Töregene.

16:35.597 --> 16:37.047
Open your hand.

16:42.707 --> 16:43.987
It's a jada stone.

16:43.987 --> 16:46.137
You can call forth storms with it.

16:46.947 --> 16:51.117
This is all I have to offer you
 as a parting gift.

16:52.417 --> 16:55.627
I really enjoyed having you in my home.

16:57.247 --> 16:58.327
Farewell.

17:00.087 --> 17:02.067
Live on with a smile on your face.

17:10.827 --> 17:14.437
It was eerily quiet that night.

17:17.137 --> 17:18.927
Ready the horses! Hurry!

17:18.927 --> 17:20.127
R-Right away!

17:25.507 --> 17:28.707
<i>The sky was burning. Soaked in blood.</i>

17:29.327 --> 17:32.497
<i>An unearthly sight the likes of which
 I had never seen before.</i>

17:32.497 --> 17:34.207
What's happening?

17:34.207 --> 17:37.337
A rebellion. The captives 
have dug in on the mountain.

17:37.727 --> 17:40.667
Prince Ögedei's army 
is moving in now to subdue them.

17:40.667 --> 17:42.757
That accursed Dayir Usun.

17:42.757 --> 17:45.597
You can never take Merkits at their word.

17:45.907 --> 17:46.947
Out of my way!

17:47.727 --> 17:48.437
Chuu!

17:48.437 --> 17:49.677
H-Hey! Wait!

17:54.397 --> 17:57.477
<i>Yes, even when the Mongols 
had shown them forgiveness...</i>

18:00.177 --> 18:03.667
<i>They had never once forgiven the Mongols.</i>

18:04.507 --> 18:06.947
We are hunters of the forest.

18:07.467 --> 18:09.987
We will never be the slaves 
of lowly sheep herders.

18:10.637 --> 18:12.957
Go and find happiness.

18:13.297 --> 18:15.877
<i>Were those words a lie as well?</i>

18:16.397 --> 18:19.337
<i>No, I'm certain he'd truly meant them.</i>

18:20.177 --> 18:23.737
<i>Which is why he hadn't told me anything.</i>

18:26.747 --> 18:31.317
<i>However, Chieftain Dayir 
made one grave oversight.</i>

18:31.837 --> 18:38.177
<i>He failed to see just 
how much I loved him.</i>

18:50.437 --> 18:52.527
Oh, I see.

18:53.587 --> 18:57.217
I'd forgotten a kam's soul 
can rise to the heavens.

18:58.117 --> 19:01.817
I only aided its escape 
by puncturing his body.

19:03.517 --> 19:05.307
A red river in the sky, huh?

19:10.597 --> 19:11.727
Who are you?

19:17.097 --> 19:19.287
What are <i>you</i> doing here?

19:19.867 --> 19:22.677
<i>The rebellion was put down all too easily.</i>

19:24.257 --> 19:28.747
<i>I later found out they'd killed Qultuqan
 and all the others.</i>

19:30.847 --> 19:36.707
<i>And upon Genghis Khan's return, 
Khulan learned of the rebellion as well.</i>

19:37.967 --> 19:40.417
<i>When she heard the news...</i>

19:43.237 --> 19:46.507
My father brought his fate 
upon himself with his folly.

19:46.507 --> 19:50.657
None can tarnish the majesty of the Khan.

19:51.847 --> 19:56.807
<i>Khulan, how could you 
wear a smile back then?</i>

19:57.437 --> 20:01.527
<i>After that, I was made Ögedei's wife 
and allowed to live.</i>

20:07.247 --> 20:09.177
<i>I gave birth to his children as well.</i>

20:10.437 --> 20:12.867
<i>Time passed by peacefully.</i>

20:13.967 --> 20:16.577
<i>Yet all that time...</i>

20:17.217 --> 20:22.167
<i>I've been waiting for a storm 
that will ravage this empire.</i>

20:23.367 --> 20:26.567
I saved you earlier because of your smile.

20:27.417 --> 20:30.387
I saw Khulan from that day in you.

20:30.637 --> 20:32.387
After all this time, I now understand.

20:32.387 --> 20:35.887
How sad and powerless 
she must have felt underneath it.

20:36.687 --> 20:40.887
But she fully understood 
what her own role was.

20:41.277 --> 20:45.397
Back then, I should've known exactly
how she was feeling, and yet...

20:48.077 --> 20:49.277
So?

20:49.687 --> 20:51.487
Who are you, really?

20:52.367 --> 20:53.617
I'm...

20:54.517 --> 20:55.587
It matters not.

20:56.247 --> 20:58.647
Regardless of who you may be, you can't—

20:57.407 --> 20:59.697
Princess Sorghaghtani told me...

21:00.507 --> 21:02.497
Prince Tolui and the Great Kha'an.

21:02.497 --> 21:06.587
The imbalance between military power 
and authority is sure to bring misfortune.

21:06.887 --> 21:10.627
In other words, the empire 
has never been frailer than it is now.

21:11.107 --> 21:11.837
You're...

21:14.267 --> 21:17.267
My name is Sitara. I'm a slave.

21:17.587 --> 21:23.227
The Mongol army killed my mistress 
and stole her precious book.

21:23.227 --> 21:28.027
My final duty to her should have been 
to get her book back, and yet...

21:28.027 --> 21:31.797
The thought that blind resistance 
could cause further tragedy...

21:32.387 --> 21:36.237
That fear has caused me 
to lead a life without purpose.

21:36.917 --> 21:39.787
But this must be the moment 
I've been waiting for.

21:41.377 --> 21:43.667
What could we possibly
 hope to accomplish?

21:51.207 --> 21:52.837
I have knowledge.

21:53.987 --> 21:57.257
Let me serve you 
as your new jada stone, Highness.

21:58.267 --> 22:01.177
Please lend me your power.

22:03.327 --> 22:06.567
Let the two of us summon a storm.

22:14.657 --> 22:18.497
Translation: John K.
Timing: Andy Ellis
Editing: SMR

22:14.657 --> 22:18.497
Quality Control: Alicia Ashby
Translation Check: Sriram Gurunathan

23:37.947 --> 23:43.257
<b>Brothers</b>

23:38.967 --> 23:40.977
<i>Next time: "Brothers."</i>
